    "message": "fix(context): validate saved investigation state on read, not just on write\n\n`saveInvestigation` and `--out` both check the bundle against\n`contextBundleSchema` before it reaches disk, but `loadInvestigation`\ntrusted a bare `as SavedInvestigation` cast. The only read-side guard was\nthe envelope check (`schema === \"ix-investigation/1\"` and a truthy\n`bundle`), so a state file with the right two fields and an arbitrary body\nwas honoured in full.\n\nThat gap is reachable: `--resume` renders the bundle, and `--diff`\nre-resolves `bundle.target.name` and sends it to the configured backend.\nThis is the read half of the same contract the write half already\nenforces.\n\nAdds a regression test whose fixture keeps the envelope deliberately\nvalid, so only bundle validation can reject it, plus a well-formed control\nso a validator that refused everything would fail instead of pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
